<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE Yoshimi-data>
<!-- A small, faithful copy of ~/.config/yoshimi/yoshimi.banks, for tests.

     Faithful in the four ways that matter and were all got wrong at least once:
       - TWO bank roots, with the same banks in both. Yoshimi copies the
         installed library into ~/.local/share/yoshimi/found on first run, so
         its splash counts everything twice — "1822 instruments in 48 banks" is
         911 in 24, seen double.
       - banks are numbered 5, 10, 15 … not 0, 1, 2.
       - instrument slots are SPARSE, and `instrument_id` is the MIDI program
         number, which is the filename's NNNN minus one.
       - a slot above 127 exists and cannot be reached by a plain program
         change (Yoshimi keeps 32 extra per bank behind an extended control).

     The two bank_root values are placeholders that test.mjs fills in, because
     a bank root is an absolute path and a fixture cannot know one. (They are
     not named here: the first version of this comment SPELLED them, and a
     String.replace hit the comment instead of the data.) -->
